---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = "/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend";
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS to Omnisend: Shopify migration decisions";
const desc = "Evaluate Omnisend\u2019s channel workflow, available migration records and documented Yotpo Loyalty connection before moving store messaging.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can Omnisend still automatically sync contacts from Yotpo?",
    "answer": "Its current migration guide says the automated Yotpo contact sync is no longer available. Inspect any previously synced records or accessible exports rather than planning on a new sync."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does the Yotpo Loyalty connection work on every plan?",
    "answer": "The current Omnisend guide specifies a Yotpo Loyalty Platinum or Enterprise requirement for the webhook field. Verify your plan and connection before relying on loyalty-triggered messages."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>The comparison has become a migration decision</h2>
      <p>Yotpo Email & SMS is retired. Its live lifecycle notice says the dashboard and associated background services are inactive. Keeping Yotpo Reviews or Loyalty does not restore messaging. Evaluate a replacement sender while treating those retained products as separate services; the old suite-versus-standalone recommendation no longer describes an available choice.</p>
      <h2>Choose channels by permission and purpose</h2>
      <p>Omnisend currently advertises email, SMS and web push. That makes it relevant for a store wanting coordinated channels, but the presence of a channel does not make every customer reachable. Draft a welcome or recovery journey with separate eligibility for each channel. A missing SMS opt-in should lead to an appropriate alternative or no message, rather than treating push or email as permission to text.</p>
      <h2>Read the migration guide against the live retirement notice</h2>
      <p>Omnisend’s Yotpo migration guide says automated contact sync is no longer available. It also retains manual export instructions that depend on Yotpo access. The live Yotpo notice says the dashboard is inactive, so those export steps are not an access promise. Start from exports already held or other legitimately available records, and establish support recovery options. If a sync was completed previously, inspect its records and suppressions before importing another copy.</p>
      <h2>Check Loyalty plan requirements before promising points flows</h2>
      <p>Omnisend documents a Yotpo Loyalty and Referrals integration using custom events and contact properties. Its guide specifies a Yotpo Platinum or Enterprise requirement for the webhook field. Verify eligibility before budgeting reward, birthday or tier-change messages around this route. Rehearse a points change and a redemption, then inspect customer matching and stale values. Keep existing loyalty notices under a named owner while replacement messages remain disabled.</p>
      <h2>Keep Reviews as its own post-purchase decision</h2>
      <p>Retaining Yotpo Reviews is compatible with treating messaging as a separate purchase, but the Loyalty connector is not proof of review-event coverage. Inventory review collection, display and any review-based targeting independently. Confirm the supported Reviews configuration needed for a proposed Omnisend workflow. If review requests remain in Yotpo Reviews, exclude a second request from the Omnisend post-purchase series and use that series for useful product education instead.</p>
      <h2>Validate the channel fallback and cost together</h2>
      <p>For a proposed recovery rehearsal, include an email-only subscriber, an eligible SMS subscriber and a customer who purchases after entry. Inspect pending sends and channel exits before activation. Budget the actual email allowance, SMS destinations, retained modules and onboarding work using current terms. Web push is not automatically free recovery or guaranteed incremental revenue; its value depends on permission and the messages your store can maintain.</p>
      <h2>Reconstruct the program from accessible records</h2>
      <p>Start with prior exports, saved templates, consent evidence, suppression records and Shopify data you can legitimately access. Do not promise a fresh export from the retired Yotpo dashboard. Ask support what recovery remains possible before setting a launch date. A customer email or phone number in an order record does not establish marketing permission. Preserve opt-outs and mark unknown consent for review rather than importing every customer as subscribed.</p>
      <h2>Activate against a message ownership map</h2>
      <p>List welcome, cart, checkout recovery, post-purchase education, review collection, loyalty notices and winback separately. Prepare replacement messages disabled and inspect purchase exits, opt-outs and missing fields before activation. Give each trigger one live owner, including Shopify automations and retained Yotpo modules. Record who can pause each sender if a customer receives the wrong sequence. These are proposed acceptance exercises, not tests we ran or evidence of revenue lift.</p>
      <h2>Primary sources</h2>
      <p>Product information checked November 25, 2026. <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo lifecycle notice</a> · <a class="link" href="https://www.omnisend.com/shopify-email-marketing/">Omnisend Shopify and channels</a> · <a class="link" href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/12048785-migrate-from-yotpo-to-omnisend">Yotpo migration guide</a> · <a class="link" href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/5967363-integrate-yotpo-loyalty-and-referrals-with-omnisend">Loyalty connection requirements</a></p>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Omnisend vs Yotpo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-klaviyo">Yotpo vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/reviews-and-ugc">Reviews & UGC playbook</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/home-goods">Email apps for home goods stores</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Migration questions" />
</BaseLayout>
